   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pppppppp/8/3nP3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 2 3",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop jumps to c4, hitting the knight — but this is the Alekhine's game. The knight retreats to b6, its ideal square, and the bishop must move again, having gained nothing.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "In the Alekhine the knight belongs on b6 — let it be chased there and the attacker loses time.",
   "plans": "Retreat to b6, then strike the centre."
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 961,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pppppppp/1n6/4P3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 3 4",
   "line": [
    "Nb6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 975,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pppppppp/1n6/4P3/8/8/PPPPBPPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [
    "Be2"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop drops back to e2, a passive post — and that is the signal to press. White has spent moves shuffling the bishop while building no real centre.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "When the opponent's pieces retreat without a plan, seize the initiative.",
   "plans": "Challenge the centre before White consolidates."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 1005,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1n1p4/4P3/8/8/PPPPBPPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The most accurate move is the pawn to d6, striking at the e5-pawn. The knight to c6 is playable, but with White holding so little of the centre there is no reason not to challenge it directly.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Attack an overextended centre at once rather than developing around it.",
   "plans": "Trade on e5 and expose the weakness."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 1015,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/ppp1pppp/1n1p4/4P3/3P4/8/PPP1BPPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5",
