   "line": [
    "dxe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Take on e5 and steer for the trade of queens. If White recaptures on the knight, the knight takes d4 and wins; and once the queens come off, the pawn on e5 becomes a huge, permanent weakness — the whole point of the Alekhine laid bare.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "The Alekhine's payoff: provoke the big centre, trade down, and target the overextended pawn.",
   "plans": "Trade queens, then win or tie White to the e5-pawn."
  },
