   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "A key restraint: do NOT simply grab on f3 and then take e5 — that drops the b7-pawn. Making the pawn a lasting weakness and tying White to its defence is often stronger than winning it outright and freeing White's pieces.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "A fixed weakness you pressure can be worth more than the pawn itself — restraint over greed.",
   "plans": "Pile on e5; don't release the tension prematurely."
  },
